\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 The ceremony ended and the room went back to being a bar.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It did not thin out. Nothing in the Clambake ever thinned out; it redistributed, and it redistributed now into a churn between the spa bath and the bar, with a hard eddy where the currents met and nobody could get through holding a full glass. The staircase was occupied to the turn. The mezzanine was occupied. There were Elvi up there who had not been able to see any of it and had cheered every word.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It was a wake and it was a coronation and nobody had told the room which, so it was being both, a few metres apart. Two Blue Hawaiis were laughing so hard that one had to take the other\u8217 ?s sleeve to stay upright. Close enough to touch, a Tulsa wept into a beer with somebody\u8217 ?s hand flat on the back of his neck, and neither found the other odd.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Walk,\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?I\u8217 ?ve only just sat down.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?You\u8217 ?ve been sitting down since Monday. You\u8217 ?ll seize.\u8221 ? Kathy took the glass out of Sarah\u8217 ?s hand and put it somewhere it would not be seen again. \u8220 ?Ten minutes. Then the chair\u8217 ?s yours and I\u8217 ?ll defend it with my body.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?She wants you to look at something,\u8221 ? said Hayley.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?I know she does.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?I want you to walk,\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?You want both,\u8221 ? Sarah said, and put her hand out for Hayley\u8217 ?s arm.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 They went the long way, because there was no short way. Elvi parted for the Holy Momma and closed up behind her, and every second one wanted to touch the belly, and about a third asked first.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 A Clambake with grey coming through his sideburns got himself off the chesterfield in three separate movements, with a hand on the arm of it and a sound. Two paces on, an Elvine came up off a bar stool and stood a moment with her palm pressed into the small of her back, waiting for something to finish. Nobody looked at either. In that room it was weather.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Then Rusty Martin came off a low stool in one go, still talking, and went to the bar.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy did not stop walking. Her head turned, and stayed turned a beat past where it had any business.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile Duval had her sleeve pushed up past the elbow and her arm out, and a small audience for it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Thirty-one years,\u8221 ? she was saying. \u8220 ?Thirty-one years I\u8217 ?ve had that, and I paid a man in Bent Street to look at taking it off and he said it\u8217 ?d cost more than the wedding did.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Let me,\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile put the arm into her hands with the satisfaction of a woman who has finally found somebody qualified. There had been a name on the inside of the forearm once, in the ornate lettering that takes a good hand and a long sitting. It was a grey suggestion now. The heavy work at the edges had held on better than the rest, so what remained was an outline with the middle gone out of it, like a word rubbed off a blackboard by somebody in a hurry.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?When did it start going?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?That\u8217 ?s the thing. Fortnight? He\u8217 ?s been dead eleven years and I\u8217 ?ve looked at his name every morning since, and then a fortnight ago I\u8217 ?m washing up and I think, that\u8217 ?s odd.\u8221 ? She turned the wrist over, pleased with herself. \u8220 ?Best thing that\u8217 ?s happened to me all year, and I include getting out of Bent Street alive.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy turned the arm slightly, into the light from the bar, and did not let go of it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Any scars?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?What?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Anything you\u8217 ?ve had a long time. Old ones.\u8221 ?\
