\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 From behind them, without turning round, Sarah said: \u8220 ?Then it can be moved.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 She said it the way a person says a thing they have just this second thought of, and put no particular weight on it at all, and went on looking at the curtains.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Chanta looked at Kathy. Kathy did not look back at him, which was as close to mercy as she got.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 He was not quick. Everyone present had built their expectations accordingly, and so nobody was watching closely enough to see him do it. He looked at Betty Lee\u8217 ?s roots, and at Marguerita, and at the group by the curtains, and he counted something on his fingers, twice, and stopped counting, and put the beers down on the bar without looking where.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Oh,\u8221 ? said Chanta.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Chanta \u8212 ?\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?No, hang on.\u8221 ? He was still working. \u8220 ?Hang on.\u8221 ?\
